WikiVisage face service — third-party model weights
====================================================

STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL. Accepted by the project owner on 2026-10-16 as a known
licence risk (decision recorded in PR #116, released as v0.11.0); the terms are
summarised under "Terms" below.

Files in this directory
-----------------------

  det_500m.onnx    SCRFD-500M with 5-point keypoints (face detector)
  w600k_mbf.onnx   ArcFace MobileFaceNet, 512-dimensional (face embedding)
  SHA256SUMS       Expected SHA-256 of both files (see "Verification")

Both files come unmodified from the InsightFace `buffalo_sc` model pack:

  https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface/releases/download/v0.7/buffalo_sc.zip

Terms
-----

The InsightFace project releases its *code* under the MIT License, but states
that its pre-trained models and the training data they were built from are
available for NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH PURPOSES ONLY. These two files are such
pre-trained models. They are NOT covered by this repository's MIT licence
(see the top-level LICENSE) and are not offered under any open-source licence.

InsightFace publishes no licence file inside the model pack; the terms are
stated in the project's README (https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface).
Read them there before relying on this notice.

What this means in practice
---------------------------

* Do not use these weights for commercial purposes.
* Wikimedia Cloud Services' Terms of Use restrict hosting non-Open-Source
  software. A research-only licence may be objected to by Toolforge
  administrators; the owner has accepted that the files could be removed.
* The face service keeps its detector/embedder behind the `FaceBackend`
  interface in `model-server/backend.py`, so a permissively licensed pair
  (for example YuNet + SFace) can replace these files without touching the
  KServe envelope, `face_client.py`, or the database.
* Removing these files makes the face service refuse to start (it verifies
  them at load time). That is intentional: it never runs on unknown weights.

Verification
------------

`model.py` verifies the SHA-256 of both files at startup and exits on any
mismatch. CI verifies `SHA256SUMS` before running the contract tests. To
re-create or re-check the files from the official release:

  scripts/fetch_weights.sh            # download, verify, install
  scripts/fetch_weights.sh --check    # verify the committed files only

The files are ordinary git blobs (about 16 MB). Do not convert them to Git LFS:
the Toolforge build service does not support it reliably, and a pointer file
would silently break the build. CI fails if that happens.
